184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (A signalised intersection is a road junction where traffic movement is controlled using traffic signals to ensure the safe and orderly movement of vehicles and pedestrians. The performance of a signalised intersection depends on factors such as traffic volume, road geometry, signal timing, lane configuration, and traffic composition.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The Indo-HCM \(Indian Highway Capacity Manual\) provides a systematic methodology for evaluating the operational performance of intersections under Indian traffic conditions. It considers the heterogeneous nature of Indian traffic, including different vehicle types, lane-discipline characteristics, and mixed traffic behaviour.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The study of a signalised intersection using the Indo-HCM method helps determine important parameters such as capacity, saturation flow, control delay, volume-to-capacity ratio, and Level of Service \(LOS\). These measures help in identifying traffic problems and assessing the effectiveness of existing signal timings.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
